BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-199857@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260910T173000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T200000
SUMMARY:Member Meetup: The Boston Public Library 
LOCATION:Offsite: Boston Public Library
DESCRIPTION:Category: Member Mixer\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimit
 ed\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199857\n\nExperienc
 e the Boston Public Library through an evening that brings together the re
 volutionary power of the printed word and the enduring ambition of one of 
 America’s great civic landmarks.\n\nBegin with a private viewing of Decl
 arations: Printing a New Nation at the Leventhal Map & Education Center. F
 or the first time\, eight rare printings of the Declaration of Independenc
 e are presented together\,illuminating how the news of American independen
 ce spread across the nation in the summer of 1776. With the exhibit closin
 g on September 13th\, this is a final opportunity to experience these docu
 ments side by side.\n\nThe evening continues with a welcome reception of d
 rinks and light bites\, followed by a private guided tour of the historic 
 McKim Building. Welcomed by Boston Public Library President\, David Leonar
 d\, and Boston Public Library Fund Executive Director\, Paula Sakey\, memb
 ers will explore the art\, architecture\, and legacy of America’s first 
 large free municipal library and get an inside look at what’s next for o
 ne of Boston’s most treasured spaces.\n\n*This event is complimentary an
 d reserved for members only. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made 
 at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199857
CATEGORIES:Member Mixer
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-199491@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260910T180000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260910T193000
SUMMARY:'Quin Chat: The Art of Coexistence
LOCATION:The Reading Room
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Chat\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: You are
  on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199491\n\
 n6:00PM Reception\, 6:30PM Discussion\nWhat does it mean for humans and w
 ildlife to thrive together in an increasingly interconnected world? Coinci
 ding with the arrival of The Great Elephant Migration in Boston\, this '
 Quin Chat brings together visionary voices at the forefront of conservatio
 n\, research\, and environmental storytelling for an evening of compelling
  conversation.\n\nModerated by 'Quin Co-Founder and philanthropist\, Sandy
  Edgerley\, together with Founder of The Great Elephant Migration\, Ruth G
 anesh and leading scholar of human-wildlife coexistence\, Dr. Tarsh Thekae
 kara\, the discussion will explore the ideas driving one of the world's mo
 st ambitious conservation initiatives.\n\nFrom restoring critical habitats
  and protecting biodiversity to reimagining the relationship between peopl
 e and the natural world\, look forward to a conversation that examines how
  innovation\, collaboration\, and community are reshaping the future of co
 nservation.\n\n*This event is complimentary and reserved for members only
 . Complimentary light bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly as
 k that all cancellations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of t
 he event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199491
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Chat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-199492@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260914T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260914T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260914T190000
SUMMARY:Earthshot Innovation Challenge Pitch Competition 
LOCATION:The Pub
DESCRIPTION:Category: ‘Quin Impact Fund\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: 
 You are on Waitlist\nEvent URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/19
 9492\n\n5:00PM Reception\, 5:30PM Program\nBefore the spotlight turns to t
 he annual Earthshot Innovation Challenge Award Ceremony at the John F. Ken
 nedy Presidential Library this winter\, The 'Quin Impact Fund invites memb
 ers to an exclusive first look at the next generation of climate innovatio
 n.\n\nDuring this special preview\, Earthshot Innovation Challenge semi-fi
 nalists will present their breakthrough concepts\, sharing bold ideas desi
 gned to address some of the world's most pressing environmental challenges
 . Members will hear each pitch\, engage with the ideas\, and cast their vo
 tes in real time to select the solution they wish to propel into the chall
 enge finals\, securing at least $25\,000 in grant funding\, and raising th
 eir chances to be awarded the top prize of $100\,000.\n\nThis exclusive ev
 ent offers a unique opportunity to experience the innovation process first
 hand while helping elevate promising solutions before they take the stage 
 at the formal competition. Be among the first to discover the visionary en
 trepreneurs shaping a more sustainable future - and play a role in recogni
 zing the ideas with the greatest potential to create lasting impact.\n\n*T
 his event is complimentary and reserved for members only. Complimentary l
 ight bites and refreshments will be served. We kindly ask that all cancel
 lations be made at least 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199492
CATEGORIES:‘Quin Impact Fund
END:VEVENT
