BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-199493@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260915T190000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260915T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260915T200000
SUMMARY:Author's Circle Book Club: "Damaged Goods" With Paul Scheufele
LOCATION:The Muse
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimited\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199493\n\nThis Septembe
 r\, join us for a thoughtful discussion on Damaged Goods\, a compelling wo
 rk of literary fiction that explores family\, loss\, and the unexpected wa
 ys grief can reshape our lives. When Brendan O'Shay inherits custody of hi
 s late sister's frozen eggs\, he and his family are forced to confront dif
 ficult questions about love\, legacy\, and what it truly means to honor so
 meone's memory.\n\nSet against the backdrop of the 2008 financial crisis i
 n New England\, Damaged Goods is an emotionally resonant novel that examin
 es the delicate balance between ambition and compassion. Rich with moral c
 omplexity and unforgettable characters\, it is an ideal choice for readers
  who enjoy thought-provoking stories that spark meaningful conversation.\n
 \nJoined by the author himself\, Paul Scheufele\, and in conversation with
  Wendy Dodson\, owner of Hummingbird Book\, the evening will explore the n
 ovel’s inspirations\, themes\, and enduring questions. Members will have
  the opportunity to engage directly with the author in an intimate convers
 ation that brings the story vividly to life.\n\n*This event is complimenta
 ry and reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshmen
 ts will be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 
 24 hours prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/199493
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:quin-event-200335@thequinhouse.com
DTSTAMP:20260917T170000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260917T183000
SUMMARY:Author Talk: "Driven" With Architect Patrick Ahearn 
LOCATION:Scottie's
DESCRIPTION:Category: The Arts\nPrice: Free / Included\nStatus: unlimited\n
 Event URL: https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/200335\n\n5:00PM Recept
 ion\, 5:30PM Discussion\nJoin award-winning classical architect and impass
 ioned car collector Patrick Ahearn for an exclusive pre-launch discussion 
 of his forthcoming book\, Driven: The Road to Iconic Design. At the inters
 ection of his two greatest passions\, architecture and automobiles\, Drive
 n explores Ahearn’s lifelong pursuit of the extraordinary through bespok
 e carriage houses that distinguish many of his legacy properties and class
 ic cars that have influenced his design purview.\n\nThrough more than a do
 zen signature projects\, Ahearn reveals carriage houses that function as e
 legant entertaining spaces\, guest retreats\, anglers’ lounges\, collect
 or’s galleries\, and more. Cars of significance are woven within the nar
 rative and photographed against the backdrop of Ahearn’s homes\, creatin
 g a compelling dialogue between forms of excellence.\n\nFeaturing captivat
 ing photography and personal narrative\, Driven is both a celebration of h
 istorically inspired architecture and a reflection on Ahearn’s remarkabl
 e design journey. Members will hear firsthand about the experiences\, infl
 uences\, automobiles\, and philosophy that have shaped his career and fuel
 ed his enduring pursuit of iconic design\n\n*This event is complimentary a
 nd reserved for members only. Complimentary light bites and refreshments w
 ill be served. We kindly ask that all cancellations be made at least 24 ho
 urs prior to the start of the event.
URL:https://members.thequinhouse.com/events/200335
CATEGORIES:The Arts
END:VEVENT
